  "name": "The Sum of the Interior Angles of a Quadrilateral",
  "problem": "The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides equals \n\n$$\n180^\\circ \\cdot (n-2).\n$$\n\nEvery quadrilateral has $n={\\color{blue}4}$ sides. Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula tells us that the sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral equals $360^\\circ.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14186732/assets/a0d6cd7aa4b4e7aba6451b32087fa6cf86e0f63d2ff70e68328a5ac9d4eddcfc.png)",
